          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 13, Q7). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t13-q008",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Synonyms",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Determine the precise contextual meaning of a specific word or phrase",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 13 · Q8",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Synonyms — Q8",
          "passage": "The following text is adapted from Willa\nCather's 1912 novel Alexander's Bridge.\nFor the next few days Alexander was very busy.\nHe took a desk in the office of a [Scottish]\nengineering firm on Henrietta Street, and was at\nwork almostconstantly. He avoided the clubs\nand usually dined alone at his hotel.",
