          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 13 · Q14",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Synonyms — Q14",
          "passage": "The following text is adapted from Kenneth\nGrahame's 1908 novelThe Wind in the Willows.\nThe Mole has been found by a friend after\ngetting lost in the woods.\nIt is beginning to snow. The Mole saw the wood\nthat had been so dreadful to him in quite a\nchanged aspect. Holes, hollows, pools, pitfalls,\nand other menaces to the wayfarer were\nvanishing fast, and a gleaming carpet was\nspringing up everywhere, that looked too\ndelicate to be trodden upon by rough feet.",
