          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Synonyms — Q15",
          "passage": "The following text is adapted from Virginia\nWoolf's 1919 novelNight and Day.Katharine is\nthe granddaughter of a celebrated poet.\n[Katharine's] descent from [a celebrated poet]\nwas no surprise to her, but matter for\nsatisfaction, until, as the years wore on, certain\ndrawbacks made themselves verymanifest.\nPerhaps it is a little depressing to inherit not\nlands but an example of intellectual virtue;\nperhaps the conclusiveness of a great ancestor is\na little discouraging to those who run the risk of\ncomparison with him.",
