          "passage": "The following text is from Kenneth Grahame's\n1908 novelThe Wind in the Willows.The Mole\nis returning home after a visit to Mr. Badger's\nhouse.\nAs he hurried along, eagerlyanticipating the\nmoment when he would be at home again\namong the things he knew and liked, the Mole\nsaw Clearly that he was an animal of tiled field\nand hedge-row, linked to the ploughed furrow,\nthe frequented pasture, the lane of evening\nlingerings, the cultivated garden-plot.",
