          "passage": "The following text is adapted from John\nMatheus's 1925 short story \"Fog.\" A train has\nstopped at a station, where heavy fog has set in.\nThe little conductor stood on tiptoe in an effort\nto keep one hand on the signal rope, craning his\nneck in a vain and dissatisfied endeavor to pierce\nthe miasma of the fog. The motorman chafed in\nhis box, thinking of the drudging lot of the\nlaboring man. Heregistered discontent.",
